{
 "about": "QuestPump's telemetry catalog (contract/telemetry-api.yaml is the design; David, 2026-10-12: \"lets do a full telemetry pass and implementation for questpump\", choosing crash reports, usage analytics like learnclash and anonymous counts). The one source of every name that leaves a device: the purposes and their switches, the Google Analytics events, parameters, values and user properties the phones may log, the screens a screen_view may name, the anonymous count points every app sends to the report Worker, and the crash context words. tools/telemetry.py writes the apps' and the Worker's catalogs from it (make telemetry) and `make check` fails on a stale one and on a parameter, blob or double whose name the never list holds; the apps name events and points only through their catalog's types, and drop a value outside it (a debug build stops on it), as the Worker refuses one. A point grows only at its end, and a double renamed in place keeps its old name in the point's `was` (old name to new, its column unchanged): the Worker reads an older app's point under the new name and fills a double a newer catalog grew at the point's end, which that point lacks, with 0 (slice 42's fix round, 2026-10-17). Every value is from a closed list or a bounded number; nothing here carries a count the player typed, a record, health data, a name or free text.",
 "purposes": {
  "crash": {
   "switch": "menu.crash",
   "about": "Crash reports (contract/crash-api.yaml)."
  },
  "usage": {
   "switch": "menu.usage",
   "about": "Usage statistics: the phones' Google Analytics events and user properties, and every app's anonymous counts. A point marked fitness goes from a phone only while the player's own answer is on (Apple 5.1.3: fitness-context data only with permission), from the desktop app while the switch reads on."
  }
 },
